agement\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nEmergency Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nPrevious Slide\nNext Slide\nExpertise for Middle-of-the-Night Emergencies and Advanced Specialty Care\nYou can trust the highly trained team at MedVet Cincinnati to serve as an extension of your family veterinarian’s care. Our hospital offers the most comprehensive, state-of-the-art emergency and specialty veterinary care in Greater Cincinnati.\nServing more than 27,000 patients a year, our team is the trusted choice for family veterinarians and pet lovers. We know pets are an important part of your family, and we strive to provide exceptional care while showing compassion for you and your pet. Our team has the expertise to diagnose and treat your pet, giving the best chance for a positive outcome.\nIf your pet is facing an emergency, you can come directly to our hospital – no appointment is needed. Our expert team is available for pet emergencies 24 hours a day, 365 days a year.\nMedVet Cincinnati Caregivers\nSearch by Name\nFilter by Specialty\nAll Specialties\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nEmergency Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSurgery\nOur Hospital Leaders\nJennifer Wells, DVM, DACVIM (SAIM)\nMedical Director\nHeidi Hill, MA, CVPM\nHospital Director\nOur Doctors\nSarah Abdelmessih\n, DVM, MS\nEmergency Medicine\nHeidi Anderson\n, DVM\nSurgery\nKaitlynn C. Ban\n, DVM, Residency Trained in Veterinary Anesthesia & Analgesia\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nMatthew Baron-Chapman\n, DVM, DACVR\nRadiology\nRush Basinger\n, DVM\nSurgery\nCaroline Billings\n, DVM, PhD\nCardiology\nLauren Blodgett\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nDawna Boudot\n, 